# WCAG contrast — Command Center chrome

> **ABSOLUTE**: Text on Command Center colored chrome (status bar, accent fills, primary-on-accent labels) MUST meet [WCAG 2.2](https://www.w3.org/TR/WCAG22/) contrast.

## Thresholds

| Text | Minimum ratio |
|------|----------------|
| Normal text (status bar labels) | **4.5:1** (AA) |
| Accent used as body text on `--bg` | **7:1** (AAA) |

## Status bar (footer)

The footer background is **`var(--accent)`** (after `themeAccentFill`). Ink MUST be `statusbarInk(fill)` from that same hex, not `theme.statusbarBg`. Light macOS blue (`#64d2ff`) → **dark** ink. Never near-white letters on that fill.

## Enforcement

- `crates/ax-web/web-ui/src/lib/themes.test.ts` W8–W10
- `bash tools/gauntlet-macos-theme.sh`

## Forbidden

- White / `#f3f3f3` on macOS system blue when dark ink meets AA
- Darkening `--accent` only so white labels pass (`ensureWhiteOnFill` on the status bar)
